{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"metadata":{"title":"EntityCollapse","roleHeading":"Enumeration","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence14EntityCollapseO","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Type Methods","anchor":"Type-Methods"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Why the hook takes the whole collection","level":2,"anchor":"Why-the-hook-takes-the-whole-collection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A per-ID resolver would only handle half the problem. Rows sharing an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are one failure mode; the other is a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"singleton"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — an entity an app holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly one of, such as a settings record. Created independently on two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fresh installs, two singletons have ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"different"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" UUIDs, so nothing groups","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them and no ID-keyed resolver can ever see the conflict. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"([E]) -> [E]"},{"text":" hook covers both, plus general garbage collection, with one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"API.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-determinism-requirement","type":"heading","text":"The determinism requirement"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A resolver must be a pure function of "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"replicated content"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"persistentModelID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", never a local timestamp, never array position. Every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"device must compute the same survivor set from the same rows. A resolver"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that doesn’t reintroduces the mutual-tombstone loss the write path is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"designed to avoid: two devices pick different survivors, each tombstones the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other’s, and after sync "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"both"}]},{"type":"text","text":" rows are gone."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It must also be idempotent — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse(collapse(rows))"},{"text":" must keep the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"IDs as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse(rows)"},{"type":"text","text":". This is checked with an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assert"},{"type":"text","text":" in debug builds."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Collapse removes IDs, not rows","type":"heading","anchor":"Collapse-removes-IDs-not-rows","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A resolver’s output is read as ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the set of IDs that should exist and what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each should contain"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":". An ID the resolver drops is deleted, including every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row carrying it. Several rows that share a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"surviving","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ID are all updated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the survivor’s value, and none of them is deleted.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That asymmetry is deliberate, and it is the whole reason the singleton case"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the one this hook really solves. Deleting an ID is safe because "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replicated: every device independently computes the same set of doomed IDs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and issues the same deletions. Deleting one of several rows that share an ID"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" safe — nothing replicated distinguishes them, so two devices can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pick different physical rows to keep, each tombstones the other’s, and both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are lost."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rows sharing an ID need no deletion anyway: writes already converge across"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every matching row and reads already collapse to one value per ID (see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB"},{"type":"text","text":"), so duplicates cost storage and nothing else."}]}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"SwiduxPersistence"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse/byID(preferring:)":{"title":"byID(preferring:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"byID","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"preferring","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ([","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]) -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse\/byid(preferring:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Collapses rows sharing an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" down to one, keeping the winner of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"choose"},{"type":"text","text":". Rows with unique IDs pass through untouched."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse","title":"EntityCollapse","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/PersistableModel":{"title":"PersistableModel","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The generated SwiftData "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" shadow for a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableEntity","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistableModel","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistablemodel","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistableModel"}]},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityDB":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitydb","title":"EntityDB","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A generic "},{"code":"@ModelActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that reads and writes any "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"kind":"symbol"}}}